# LeadPipe context discipline

Lead data must not enter the chat context. Use LeadPipe MCP (`lp_plan`, `lp_run`, `lp_status`, `lp_inventory`, `lp_sample`, `lp_export`).

- No paging vendor APIs for contacts/companies in this conversation.
- No pasting CSV / JSON lead lists into messages or tool args.
- `lp_sample` max 10 rows; everything else is counts, job IDs, signed URLs.
- Always pass `client_tag`. Cost-gate paid jobs with `approve_cost_usd`.
- Smartlead restore/requeue → `import_smartlead` from storage, not chat imports.

If LeadPipe tools are missing, tell the user to wire the MCP server — do not work around by loading rows into context.

See `leadpipe/CLAUDE.md` for tool mapping and examples.
